== 3.9 Chapter 3 Practice Drill — 30 Questions

30 questions graded in the order the CBT engine is likely to meet them. Allow 33 minutes; the key and a full solution for every question follow.

#mcq(1, [The hormone that lowers blood glucose is],
  [insulin],
  [thyroxine],
  [glucagon],
  [adrenaline]
)

#mcq(2, [Endocrine glands are described as ductless because they],
  [produce enzymes only],
  [have no blood supply],
  [secrete their hormones directly into the blood],
  [secrete through a tube onto the skin]
)

#mcq(3, [The hormone that increases water reabsorption in the kidney is],
  [insulin],
  [oestrogen],
  [glucagon],
  [ADH]
)

#mcq(4, [A shoot bends towards light because auxin],
  [collects on the shaded side and makes those cells elongate],
  [moves down to the roots],
  [collects on the lit side and makes those cells elongate],
  [is destroyed on the shaded side]
)

#mcq(5, [The master gland of the endocrine system is the],
  [pancreas],
  [thyroid],
  [pituitary],
  [adrenal]
)

#mcq(6, [Diabetes mellitus is caused by a shortage of],
  [thyroxine],
  [insulin],
  [glucagon],
  [ADH]
)

#mcq(7, [Adrenaline is secreted by the],
  [pancreas],
  [adrenal medulla],
  [thyroid],
  [pituitary]
)

#mcq(8, [Which of these is an effect of adrenaline?],
  [Constriction of the pupils],
  [Increased heart rate and breathing rate],
  [Decreased blood glucose],
  [Slower heart rate]
)

#mcq(9, [Goitre is caused by a deficiency of],
  [iron],
  [vitamin C],
  [calcium],
  [iodine]
)

#mcq(10, [A hormone is best defined as],
  [an enzyme that digests food],
  [a substance secreted through a duct onto the skin],
  [a nerve impulse],
  [a chemical secreted by a ductless gland and carried in the blood to a target organ]
)

#mcq(11, [Glucagon acts by],
  [speeding up metabolism],
  [converting glycogen to glucose in the liver],
  [increasing water reabsorption],
  [converting glucose to glycogen]
)

#mcq(12, [Too little growth hormone in childhood causes],
  [gigantism],
  [dwarfism],
  [goitre],
  [diabetes]
)

#mcq(13, [The islets of Langerhans are found in the],
  [thyroid],
  [pancreas],
  [liver],
  [kidney]
)

#mcq(14, [Which hormone is secreted in greater quantity when a person is dehydrated?],
  [Oestrogen],
  [Glucagon],
  [Insulin],
  [ADH]
)

#mcq(15, [Phototropism is a response to],
  [light],
  [water],
  [touch],
  [gravity]
)

#mcq(16, [Auxin is produced mainly in the],
  [root cap],
  [flower petal],
  [shoot tip],
  [leaf mesophyll]
)

#mcq(17, [Which of these is a plant hormone?],
  [Thyroxine],
  [Insulin],
  [Auxin],
  [Adrenaline]
)

#mcq(18, [In a root, a high concentration of auxin],
  [stimulates elongation],
  [destroys the root],
  [has no effect],
  [inhibits elongation]
)

#mcq(19, [The hormone that stimulates the thyroid gland is],
  [insulin from the pancreas],
  [TSH from the pituitary],
  [thyroxine from the thyroid],
  [ADH from the pituitary]
)

